	(text "PHASE CONFIGURATION  (U1 = controller, U4 = follower)\n\nDUAL PHASE (default - U1 + U4 fitted)\n  R74  DNP      U1 MSEL2 open -> 2-phase stack\n  R75  FIT 0R   VSHARE U1 <-> U4\n  R76  FIT 0R   PWR_EN -> U4 EN/UVLO\n  R77  DNP\n  R16  FIT      U4 AVIN\n\nSINGLE PHASE (U1 only)\n  R74  FIT 0R   U1 MSEL2 -> AGND1 = stand-alone\n  R75  DNP      isolate VSHARE\n  R76  DNP\n  R77  FIT 0R   hold U4 EN/UVLO low (only if U4 fitted)\n  R16  DNP      optional, removes U4 AVIN\n  U4, L2 and U4 support parts may be left DNP\n\nNOTES\n- NEVER fit R76 and R77 together (shorts PWR_EN to GND).\n- U1 checks the stack at power-up: a mismatch between the\n  MSEL2 strap and the follower gives a POR fault.\n- BCX and SYNC stay connected in both modes (TI SLUUC47A 4.5).\n- Firmware must match the mode: STACK_CONFIG (0xEC),\n  COMPENSATION_CONFIG (0xB1) and IOUT_OC limits. Stored\n  STACK_CONFIG overrides the pin strap unless\n  PIN_DETECT_OVERRIDE (0xEE) bit 12 is set."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
